TI  - Indwelling pleural catheter for outpatient management of tuberculous empyema.
LID - 10.1136/bcr-2019-233213 [doi]
LID - e233213
AB  - The use of indwelling pleural catheters (IPC) is well established in the 
      treatment of malignant pleural effusions. They allow symptom management with 
      intermittent drainage without requiring overnight admission to hospital. However, 
      little is known about their effectiveness in the treatment of pleural infections. 
      Here, we present a case where an IPC is used in the therapeutic management of 
      tuberculous empyema. The IPC enabled outpatient treatment, allowed the patient to 
      return to work and reduced the cost of treatment and the risk of 
      hospital-acquired complications.
