DP  - 2020 Jul
TI  - High-pressure leakage of pleural fluid through the healed entry site of the 
      indwelling pleural catheter from undrained locules.
PG  - e00587
LID - 10.1002/rcr2.587 [doi]
LID - e00587
AB  - The indwelling pleural catheter (IPC) is an established treatment for recurrent 
      pleural effusion. Fluid leakage through the IPC insertion tract has been 
      reported, but its occurrence is only limited to a short period after the 
      procedure. Besides, the drainage efficacy of IPC may be limited by the presence 
      of loculation in the pleural space, especially when intrapleural fibrinolytic is 
      contraindicated. We report a case of fluid leakage through the healed entry site 
      of IPC due to high pressure built from undrained pleural fluid locules, which was 
      successfully treated with an additional drain targeting the largest undrained 
      locule.
